Here's the TUnit lifecycle at each scope:

## 1. Before/After every individual test in a class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // runs after each test
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_WithNoItems_Throws() { /* ... */ }
}
```

You can also use the **constructor** or implement `IDisposable`/`IAsyncDisposable`.

## 2. Once before first / after last test in a class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // static — runs once before first test in this class
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once after last test in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task PlaceOrder_Succeeds() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 3. Once before/after all tests in the assembly

```csharp
// Can live in any file in the assembly
public class GlobalSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once before any test in this assembly
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once after all tests in this assembly complete
    }
}
```

## 4. Once for the entire test session (cross-assembly)

```csharp
public class TestRunLifecycle
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        // very first thing — before any assembly starts
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDownDatabase(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        // very last thing — after everything finishes
    }
}
```

---

### Quick-reference table

| Scope | Before | After |
|-------|--------|-------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` | `[After(Test)]` |
| Class (once) | `[Before(Class)]` (static) | `[After(Class)]` (static) |
| Assembly (once) | `[Before(Assembly)]` (static) | `[After(Assembly)]` (static) |
| Session (once) | `[Before(TestSession)]` (static) | `[After(TestSession)]` (static) |

**Bonus:** `[BeforeEvery(Test)]` / `[AfterEvery(Test)]` (and `Class`/`Assembly` variants) are **global** cross-cutting hooks that fire for *every* test/class regardless of which class they're declared in — handy for logging or diagnostics.

All hooks can be `async Task`, accept a context parameter, and optionally take a `CancellationToken`.
